---
const { race } = Astro.props;
---
<section class="faq" id="faq">
  <div class="wrap faq-wrap">
    <div class="reveal">
      <div class="kicker">Race Logistics</div>
      <h2 class="sec-title">Common <em>questions</em>.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-list">
      <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q">Are pace groups guaranteed?<span class="pm"></span></button><div class="faq-a"><p>Yes. Pace groups run from 3:00 to 5:00 every 15 minutes (3:00, 3:15, 3:30… through 5:00). Each group has one lead pacer and one sweep pacer. Both wear bib numbers showing their target finish time and carry visible signs through mile 24.</p></div></div>
      <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q">What's the qualifying time policy for the Sub-Elite Corral?<span class="pm"></span></button><div class="faq-a"><p>Submit a verified marathon finish under 3:00 (M) or 3:30 (W) from any USATF/AIMS-sanctioned race in the past 36 months. We verify within 5 business days. If accepted, you get front-corral access behind the invited elites and a dedicated warm-up area.</p></div></div>
      <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q">Where do I check my gear on race morning?<span class="pm"></span></button><div class="faq-a"><p>Gear check opens 5:30 AM at the finish line and you take it on the bus to the start. We move your bag back to the finish during the race so it's ready when you cross. Bring only one official Capital gear bag (issued at packet pickup) — anything else won't be accepted at check.</p></div></div>
      <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q">What's the weather policy?<span class="pm"></span></button><div class="faq-a"><p>Race runs in cold, rain, or moderate heat. Lightning, ice, or wet-bulb temp above 28°C triggers a modified course or delay. We email registrants by 5 AM race morning if anything changes. Capital's average November race-day temperature is 47°F — built for fast.</p></div></div>
      <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q">Can I defer my entry if I'm injured?<span class="pm"></span></button><div class="faq-a"><p>Yes. Defer once to next year for $25 by October 1, no questions asked. Two deferrals max. After October 1, no deferrals — entries are non-refundable per the terms you agreed to at registration.</p></div></div>
      <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q">Are the elevation profile and certification real?<span class="pm"></span></button><div class="faq-a"><p>Yes. The course is USATF-certified (#MA-25-CFM, renewed annually). Elevation profile is from the certification survey — accurate to within ±5 ft. Boston Athletic Association accepts Capital times for BQ qualification.</p></div></div>
      <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q">How do I get my finish photos?<span class="pm"></span></button><div class="faq-a"><p>Free for personal use. Search your bib at the gallery link emailed Sunday night. Pro photographers shoot start, mile 13, mile 20, and finish line. High-res downloads no watermark.</p></div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
